Agency enabler #4 (issue #4): xdg_popup on wlr-layer-shell surfaces.

Lets a Views menu/tooltip/bubble whose parent is a WaylandLayerShellWindow (the
bar/dock) actually create its xdg_popup. Upstream WaylandWindow::GetXdgParentWindow
skips any parent that is neither toplevel nor popup (a layer window is neither) and
XdgPopup::Initialize then finds no parent xdg_surface -> LOG(ERROR)/CHECK-abort. The
wlr protocol answer (wlr-layer-shell-unstable-v1.xml, get_popup) is: create the
xdg_popup with a NULL xdg parent, then call zwlr_layer_surface_v1.get_popup to parent
it onto the layer surface, both BEFORE the popup's initial commit.

Three upstream files, all in regions disjoint from the earlier layer-shell patches:
  - wayland_window.h  : unconditional fwd-decl + virtual As* down-cast (base nullptr).
  - wayland_window.cc : base As* impl (nullptr) + GetXdgParentWindow loop stop.
  - xdg_popup.cc      : guarded includes + Initialize NULL-parent + get_popup branch.
The window.h/.cc additions are unguarded no-ops when the flag is off (no window is
ever a layer window); the xdg_popup.cc branch is compiled out entirely.

WIRE ORDER (apply strictly in sequence, all against the same c150 base tree):
  agency-source.patch
    -> agency-layershell-factory-fix.patch
      -> agency-layershell-popup.patch   (THIS patch)
This patch's window.h/.cc hunks are disjoint from agency-source's, and it shares no
file with factory-fix, so it applies cleanly last.

diff --git a/ui/ozone/platform/wayland/host/wayland_window.cc b/ui/ozone/platform/wayland/host/wayland_window.cc
index 6256206..8542139 100644
--- a/ui/ozone/platform/wayland/host/wayland_window.cc
+++ b/ui/ozone/platform/wayland/host/wayland_window.cc
@@ -1084,7 +1084,13 @@ WaylandWindow* WaylandWindow::GetTopMostChildWindow() {
 WaylandWindow* WaylandWindow::GetXdgParentWindow() {
   auto* xdg_parent_window = parent_window();
   while (xdg_parent_window && !xdg_parent_window->AsWaylandToplevelWindow() &&
-         !xdg_parent_window->AsWaylandPopup()) {
+         !xdg_parent_window->AsWaylandPopup() &&
+         // Agency (enabler #4): stop the walk at a layer-shell surface so it is
+         // returned as the xdg-parent instead of being skipped. Unconditional:
+         // when the layer-shell buildflag is off no window is ever a layer
+         // window, so AsWaylandLayerShellWindow() is always nullptr and this
+         // extra term is a no-op (upstream behaviour byte-identical).
+         !xdg_parent_window->AsWaylandLayerShellWindow()) {
     xdg_parent_window = xdg_parent_window->parent_window();
   }
   return xdg_parent_window;
@@ -1115,6 +1121,13 @@ WaylandToplevelWindow* WaylandWindow::AsWaylandToplevelWindow() {
   return nullptr;
 }
 
+// Agency (enabler #4): base returns nullptr; WaylandLayerShellWindow overrides
+// to return |this|. Unguarded — with the layer-shell buildflag off no subclass
+// ever overrides this, so it is behaviourally identical to upstream.
+WaylandLayerShellWindow* WaylandWindow::AsWaylandLayerShellWindow() {
+  return nullptr;
+}
